<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Franklin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1730–1813</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Franklin was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benjamin-franklin">Benjamin Franklin</a> and the last royal governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a>, from 1763 to 1776. He remained loyal to the Crown during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolution">American Revolution</a>, was arrested in 1776, and after his release led Loyalist associations in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> before settling in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-franklin.jpg" alt="William Franklin" width="299" height="361" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Mather Brown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_Franklin_painting_attributed_to_Mather_Brown.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
